module v2.std.live_tree

data live_tree_disposition_note: String = "Declared witness input-domain disposition (ROADMAP 2-host-scaffold-classifier-defork): a witness entry declares whether its evaluation reads the live host tree (filesystem/corpus state outside its resolved substrate closure). The single authority is a `data live_tree_disposition: LiveTreeDisposition = ...` row in the WITNESS ENTRY FILE itself - entry grain, so the fact holds no matter where the read hides behind imports. This dissolves the interim floor:host_scaffold marker and the Rust text classifier witness_test_fn_uses_live_host_scan (deleted with this model). TWO CONSUMERS READ THIS FACT AND THEY DEFAULT SILENCE IN OPPOSITE DIRECTIONS, and an earlier revision of this row stated one of them as though it were the fact. WHAT IS TRUE: v1_compiler.cli_run parse_entry_live_tree_disposition, which feeds AFFECTED-SET SELECTION, treats an undeclared entry as ReadsLiveTree, so it never predict-skips. WHAT WAS OMITTED: v1_compiler.cli_run witness_file_from_source, the REQUIRED FLOOR's own scan and the consumer that decides whether a witness EXECUTES, fires only on a column-zero data line naming both LiveTreeDisposition and ReadsLiveTree - so on that path UNDECLARED MEANS EXECUTES. Neither reading is wrong on its own terms and that is exactly the section 3 defect: a fact with two authorities has none. The omission was load-bearing rather than cosmetic, because a reader consulting this row to answer *what happens to a witness that declares nothing* was told the fail-closed half and would conclude the witness is withheld, which is false of the consumer that runs it. A ROW THAT DECLARES SubstrateInputsOnly WHILE ACTUALLY READING LIVE STATE IS RE-CHECKED BY NOTHING, and this row previously said otherwise. It named *the nightly affected-set falsifier (predict-only cold run)* as the enforcement, promising that a lying row surfaces as a counted divergence within one cadence window. THAT CADENCE DOES NOT EXIST: falsifier.yml was deleted by the 2026-08-15 floor cut (gunbc#8283) and the repository carries three workflows, none of which runs a predict-only cold comparison. The sentence was true when written and became false when the cadence died, with nothing to notice - the stale-present-tense class DESIGN records, in an authority a reader consults first. THE SURVIVING BACKSTOP IS v2.std.effect_reach, AND IT IS NOT A SUBSTITUTE FOR THE DECLARATION. reads_live_tree_effective takes the declared answer first and falls through to effect_reach_derived_reads_live_tree_for_entry only when the row says SubstrateInputsOnly, so the derivation is the only thing standing between a lying row and a predict-skip. Its detection ceiling is declared at effect_reach_detection_ceiling and executed by the fixture pair effect_reach_conjunction_loses_a_closure_that_reads_with_no_path_literal: it classifies a closure as host-reading only when a repository path literal and a host-sink call shape BOTH occur somewhere in it, independently, so a closure that performs a real Filesystem.Read and names no path derives NOT-live. The consequence is the one that matters here and it runs the other way from the usual objection that an authored declaration duplicates a derivable fact: the derivation does not derive this fact, so the fail-closed undeclared default on the selection path is load-bearing rather than redundant, and replacing the declaration with the derivation would be a scope narrowing wearing a construction argument. STAMPING THE SILENT POPULATION WAS BUILT AND DROPPED, recorded here so the next reader does not re-propose it as though it were untried: the change existed in full - 520 witness files carrying no disposition row, each stamped, with silence made a typed located refusal on BOTH consumers so no default survived for them to disagree about - and it was discarded before review because the required floor's decline arm, the consumer that made a truthful ReadsLiveTree stamp cost anything, was already being deleted at its root in an open change. Hand-authoring 520 rows for a consumer scheduled to disappear is the redundant work DESIGN section 2 prices, and the ordering the brief assumed was backwards: the arm's deletion is what makes a truthful stamp free, so it is the enabling event and not the reward. WHAT WOULD REVIVE THE QUESTION is not the population growing but the SELECTION consumer acquiring an enforcement it does not have - if a lying SubstrateInputsOnly row can be caught again, what a silent file means becomes decidable and worth deciding; until then a stamp asserts a fact nothing checks."

data live_tree_disposition_stamp_provenance: String = "Migration stamp provenance (2026-07-11, machine-stamped batch): the initial corpus-wide SubstrateInputsOnly rows were stamped from the deleted entry-text classifier's verdict (entry file contains none of: floor:host_scaffold, layer_import_facts, _live(, _facts_live(, filesystem_read) - ENTRY-TEXT GRAIN, so they inherit that classifier's declared blind spot: a live read hidden behind an import was invisible to it (the former cli_run.rs cross-file deficit). A stamped row is therefore machine-vouched, not author-vouched. Enforcement is the nightly affected-set falsifier (counted divergence within one cadence window). Dissolves-at: G2 call-reachability live-read classification (import-closure walk over LiveReadCarrier registry + fn-arrow DependencyView) per docs/plans/live-read-witness-classification-design.md — when stamps can be re-derived from proven runtime-read closure."

type LiveTreeDisposition
  = ReadsLiveTree
  | SubstrateInputsOnly
